+# Package G: ground layer, vehicle air state, stunt jumps
+
+Branch `worktree-agent-a69e1efc71ef57b4d`. Part of HANDOFF-hill-content.md phase 3.
+
+## What is here
+- `game/scripts/ground.gd` (static, like Terrain): `Ground.height(x, z, y_hint)`,
+  `surface(x, z, base, y_hint)` (+ `hit`, `hit_grad`), `normal`, `terrain_grad`,
+  `add_strip`, `add_ramp`, `add_cut`, `remove`, `clear`, `deck`, `ids`. Decks
+  and cuts bucketed in 32 m cells; no deck in a cell = the caller's terrain
+  value after one dictionary look-up. Rules in the file header.
+- `vehicle.gd`: ground from Ground (own y as hint); air state: takes off when
+  the ground falls more than `AIR_LIFT` (0.3 m) in one frame below where
+  the car's climb and gravity carry it, flies ballistic, lands with an impact from the vertical speed
+  against the ground's slope (damage over `AIR_LAND_SAFE` 12 m/s). Signals
+  `took_off(car)`, `air_landed(car, air_time, distance, height)`;
+  `last_flight` {from, to, time, distance, height, rise, speed, impact, deck}.
+- `humanoid.gd`: feet on Ground (hint = feet y). `kits/ramp_kit.gd`: timber
+  and steel kickers (mesh, side-wall and core colliders; the deck is a
+  Ground ramp). `stunts.gd`: four ramps on Copperback Cut (bend $750, crest
+  $500, shale $400, hump $400), zones, pay once, save/load, readout.
+  `tests/ground_tests.gd`: 8 tests, in TEST_MODULES.
+
+## Decisions
+- Deck counts only at or below `y_hint + 0.6` (STEP): bridge found from
+  above, ignored from the road below; terrain always solid outside a cut.
+- Round joins only in the join's wedge (past the end of one segment and
+  before the start of the next). The first version let any segment within
+  the half width answer past its end; ramp stations (1.4 m apart, half
+  width 2.3 m) then answered for stations two away and cars took off 4 m
+  before the lip. Tests now check every ramp edge to edge against its
+  profile and a bending deck of 1.2 m segments along its middle.
+- Landing zones from probes (sports car, 16 to 42 m/s, landing distance
+  past the lip): bend 29-140 m, crest 22-109, shale 17-118, hump 26-160.
+  Zones cover 16 to about 36 m/s: bend 20-115, crest 16-92, shale 12-96,
+  hump 20-122 m, half widths 9-10 m.
+- Crest ramp moved to foot (2646.6, -3004): its run-up crossed the bend
+  ramp. `Stunts.clearings()` covers run-up, ramp and landing zone.
+
+## Traps
+- Ramps sit on the Cut's verges (3.9-4.4 m off a 6 m track): traffic and
+  races that run wide at the Copperback bend can clip the bend ramp's walls.
+- Country tiles stream trees round the player: set the clearings before
+  placing anyone at a ramp, or trees end up in the run-up.
+- Spawners that use Terrain.height directly (traffic, peds, exits) ignore
+  decks; fine for ramps, not for phase-4 bridges (see below).
+
+## Patches for the main session (not applied here)
+main.gd:
+```gdscript
+const Stunts = preload("res://scripts/stunts.gd")  # with the preloads
+var stunts  # with `var hunting`
+# replaces `Country.Tiles.clearings = Heliports.clearings()`:
+Country.Tiles.clearings = Heliports.clearings() + Stunts.clearings()
+stunts = Stunts.new()  # after `add_child(hunting)`
+stunts.game = self
+add_child(stunts)
+```
+missions/mission_manager.gd (as hunting):
+```gdscript
+# save dict, after "hunting": ..., add: "stunts": game.stunts.to_save(),
+var stunt  # load, after the hunting load = data.get("stunts")
+game.stunts.load_save(stunt if typeof(stunt) == TYPE_DICTIONARY else {})
+game.stunts.load_save({})  # reset, after game.hunting.load_save({})
+```
+hud.gd: none needed; stunts.gd calls `game.hud.show_message` ("Stunt jump
+n/N  +$prize" / "Stunt jump" / "Stunt jump missed" + readout). player.gd:
+none; stunts watches `game.player.vehicle`.
+
+## Phase 4 (bridges, tunnels)
+- Bridge: `Ground.add_strip(id, centreline, deck top heights, carriageway
+  + kerbs width, "bridge")`; piers and parapets are colliders, not the deck.
+- Tunnel: `Ground.add_cut(id, portal-to-portal centreline, roof heights,
+  bore width)` plus `add_strip` for its floor (the road's heights); walls
+  are colliders. The hill over it stays solid from above.
+- Anything placed under a bridge must pass its own height as `y_hint` (INF
+  finds the bridge). Keep under ~1000 segments per 32 m cell.
+
+## Open items
+- West Ridge Track (a track) launches a car at 25 m/s or more; Crest Drive
+  peaks at 0.19 m of lift a frame at 30 m/s (limit 0.3).
+- Landings over 12 m/s vertical hurt (42 m/s off the bend: health 71/100).
