++##
++## spec keys:
++##   length, width    the deck (m)
++##   deck             PackedFloat32Array: the deck's top at N+1 stations,
++##                    evenly spaced from the foot (0) to the lip (N)
++##   ground_l, ground_r  the ground under the deck's left (-x) and right (+x)
++##                    edges at the same stations
++##   ground_front     the ground on the centreline 4, 8 and 12 m before the
++##                    foot (painted arrows)
++##   style            "timber" (plank deck, posts and braces) or "steel"
++##                    (plate deck, hazard band at the lip, red truss)
++##
++## The deck has no collider: Ground (ground.gd) holds it as a deck and lifts
++## whatever drives or walks onto it. build() returns the colliders that keep
++## things out of the ramp's sides and back, as point clouds for
++## ConvexPolygonShape3D: a wall just outside each edge (from SINK under the
++## ground to RAIL over the deck, so it is also the side rail) and, where the
++## deck is high, a core under the deck whose top stays CORE_GAP below it. A
++## car on the ramp never reaches the core (its level hull, 3 m either side of
++## its centre on the steepest part, slope 0.35, clears it); one driving into
++## the back is stopped. Vehicles longer than that (buses) can scrape it.
